## ISS-011: Empty catch block in `GamingModeService`

### File
`/root/Redball/src/Redball.UI.WPF/Services/GamingModeService.cs`

### Original
```csharp
            try
            {
                using var proc = System.Diagnostics.Process.GetProcessById((int)processId);
                processName = proc.ProcessName;
            }
            catch { }
```

### Replacement
```csharp
            try
            {
                using var proc = System.Diagnostics.Process.GetProcessById((int)processId);
                processName = proc.ProcessName;
            }
            catch (ArgumentException)
            {
                // Process exited between detection and lookup
                processName = "Unknown";
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                Logger.Debug("GamingModeService", $"Unexpected process lookup error for PID {processId}: {ex.Message}");
                processName = "Unknown";
            }
```

### Reason
Catches only the expected `ArgumentException` (process already exited) and logs unexpected exceptions instead of silently discarding all errors.

### Verification
`dotnet build ...` and runtime test.
